{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Are the style options the words your customers use, or the words your design team uses?","Do you sell in physical stores at all? If not, the in-store follow-up can become a question about pop-ups or events.","Which buying factors would change your product or photography decisions if they ranked highly?","Is early access the right thing to offer, or would a lookbook or size advice be more welcome?"],"howToUseResponses":"Split the results by style and age group before reading anything else, since a streetwear customer and a tailoring customer rarely want the same thing. Look at what online shoppers need to feel confident: if fit reviews and body-type photos rank high, that is a product page change, not a marketing one. Use the discovery channels to decide where your next campaign budget goes.","customizeSteps":["Swap the style list for the aesthetics your collections actually cover, and add your own categories such as shoes or jewellery if they matter.","Change the early-access offer at the end to whatever you can really deliver, and say how often you will email.","Share the link from your social profiles and order confirmation emails, then export results to CSV to compare segments."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a fashion marketing questionnaire ask?","a":"Style, how often and where people shop, what they weigh when buying, how they discover brands and what they wish brands did better. Add budget only if it will change a decision."},{"q":"How do I get customers to fill in a fashion survey?","a":"Keep it short and give something real in return, like early access to a collection. Asking one question at a time in a chat also feels lighter than a long page of boxes."},{"q":"Should I ask about sustainability?","a":"Yes, but as a scale rather than a yes or no. Most people will say it matters; the useful signal is whether it actually decides the purchase."},{"q":"Can I add photos of products to the questions?","a":"You can attach an image to any question when you edit the template, which is useful if you want reactions to a specific piece or look."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":10,"title":"Fashion shopper questionnaire","description":"Understand your fashion customers' style, spending and what persuades them to buy.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_fashionm00","ref":"welcome","title":"Hi! We're a fashion brand trying to understand how you like to shop. It takes about three minutes.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_fashionm01","ref":"age_range","title":"Which age group are you in?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"dropdown","options":[{"id":"opt_under_18","label":"Under 18","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_18_to_24","label":"18 to 24","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_25_to_34","label":"25 to 34","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_35_to_44","label":"35 to 44","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_45_to_54","label":"45 to 54","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_55_or_over","label":"55 or over","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_prefer_not_to","label":"Prefer not to say","image_key":null}]},{"id":"blk_fashionm02","ref":"style","title":"Which of these describe your style? Choose up to three.","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"multi_select","options":[{"id":"opt_classic_and_timeless","label":"Classic and timeless","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_casual_and_comfortable","label":"Casual and comfortable","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_minimal","label":"Minimal","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_streetwear","label":"Streetwear","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_trend_led","label":"Trend-led","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_vintage_or_second","label":"Vintage or second-hand","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_sporty","label":"Sporty","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_workwear_and_tailoring","label":"Workwear and tailoring","image_key":null}],"minSelections":1,"maxSelections":3,"allo